  "AICL is a protocol proposal — it does not guarantee that AI companies will pay.": "AICL ukax mä protocolo amtakiwa — janiw seguruchakiti IA empresanakax pagapxaspa sasa.",
  "AICL is the licensing and transaction layer built on top of AICR. Where AICR declares what is allowed, AICL defines how permission is actually obtained: license tiers and prices, quote and payment endpoints, signed license tokens, usage and audit logs, and revocation. It is designed to interoperate with emerging machine-payment mechanisms such as HTTP 402 flows and pay-per-crawl schemes, with agentic payment kept inside human-approved budgets and audit trails.": "AICL ukax AICR patxarun jaljata licenciamiento ukat transacción capawa. AICR kunas iyawsatäki ukjay yatiyi, AICL ukhaxa permisox kunjamsa chiqapuni katuqasi ukanak qhanañchi: licencia patanaka ukat chaninakapa, jisktʼawi ukat pago punto finalanaka, firmata licencia tokennaka, apnaqäwi ukat auditoría registronaka, ukat jark'aqäwi. HTTP 402 sarawinaka ukat pay-per-crawl amtanaka kunjamtï, ukhamampi apnaqasiñataki lurata, agentenakan pagopax jaqin iyawsata presupuestonakapan ukat auditoría thakinakapan taypin imantatawa.",
