  "Content policy summary": "Contenido política resumenapa",
  "Continue to site": "Sitior sarantaña",
  "Convert rights declarations into a workable licensing market instead of a binary open/closed web.": "Derechonak yatiyawinak lurasiri licenciamiento mercadoru tukuyaña, mä ch'ulla jist'arata/jist'antata internet jan ukhama.",
  "Copied ✓": "Copiatawa ✓",
  "Copy": "Copiaña",
  "Correct positioning: independent research drafts, protocol proposals, and an open specification experiment.": "Chiqa uñacht'ayäwi: jan khitirus katuqiri yatiqäwi borradoranaka, protocolo amtanaka, ukat mä jist'arata especificación uñacht'awi.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Belgium (BE) now maps to Dutch instead of French — Flemish speakers are the country’s majority (~60%) over Walloon French speakers (~40%).": "Nayrïri qallta askichatawa: Bélgica (BE) jichhax neerlandés arur puri, francés jan ukhama — flamenco parlirinakawa markan taypin jach'a jaqinaka (~60%), francés walón parlirinakat (~40%) sipansa.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Kazakhstan (KZ) now maps to Kazakh instead of Russian, now that a Kazakh translation exists — the same kind of fix as the earlier Belgium correction.": "Nayrïri qallta askichatawa: Kazajistán (KZ) jichhax kazajo arur puri, ruso jan ukhama, kazajo tuqin mayjt'ayäwix jichhax utjatapata — Bélgica askichawi kikpacha kasta.",
  "Could AI Be Conscious?": "Could AI Be Conscious?",
  "Crawler access rules": "Rastreadoran mantawi arunaka",
  "Crawler simulator": "Rastreador simulador",
  "Currency": "Qullqi kasta",
  "Custom tier": "Kikpachanjama pata",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous ukax mä jark'aqata Journal of Medical Ethics ukaru apayat qillqatat parlaraki, kunapan walja luqata, IA alucinata sitäwinaka utjäna — jan chiqa universidad mayacht'awinakampi ukat jan apnaqasiri correo electrónico direccionanakampi. Qillqiripax askichañ atisipanxa, jan askichatäkänwa sarakïna sapxi. Aka qillqatax Bioethics ukampi mayacht'ayi, kunatï automático sitäwi uñakipäwipax akjay pantjasïw jikxataspana; ukat akham amuyti: chiqa jan atipäwix janiw detección tecnologíakiti (mä comentaristan scriptapax luqata sitäwinak mä minuto jan phuqhat qhanañchäna), jan ukasti jan pagat revisoranakan luräwipa ukat apstayäwin incentivonakapawa, walja lurañ mä uñakipat askinjam churiri.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Jan pagat datu apnaqäwi ukat waranqa waranqa millón dólar IA valoranaka",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis ukax FINRA jinaki mä regulador amtaraki, nayrïr modelonak apstawitaki: laboratorionakax modelonak uñakipañataki apayapxaspa, 30 uru jan apstawitpach nayraqata, nayraqatax munasïna, EEUU mercadon phuqhañ munata thakiru sarantasa.",
  "Denied": "Jark'aqatawa",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Apnaqasiñataki qallta política plantilla",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Apnaqasiñataki qallta política plantilla /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip ukanwa — mä pisi estático sitio, phuqhata makinanakan ullañapataki capampi, Cloudflare Pages jan ukax yaqha estático hostingtaki wakichatawa.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Jumana sitioman makinanakan ullañapataki políticanak apnaqasiña",
  "Disclaimer": "Yatiyawi",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Jaqin apnaqañapataki interfaz, SEO, jan ukax jan mayjt'ata APInakat mayjawa, AI Ingestion & Capability Layer ukax sitionakaru makina nayraqat arquitecturawa churi: Manifest capa (mantawi puntonaka kunjamtï /llms.txt ukat /ai/manifest.json), Corpus capa (makinanakan ullañapataki yatiña), Capability capa (agenten jawsañ atipiri herramientanaka), ukat Governance capa (mistuwi, licenciamiento, versionamiento). Nayraqatax estáticowa, APInakaru ukat MCPru wali askicht'ayaña atiwa. Yatiyawi: aka qillqatan AICL ukax ingestion arquitecturaru sutichi; aka sition protocolo pankanakapanx AICL ukax IA Contenido Licenciamiento Capar apayaraki.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Qillqatanaka",
  "Docs / Examples": "Qillqatanaka / Uñacht'awinaka",
  "Document library": "Qillqatanakan bibliotecapa",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "IA derechonïti — ukat kuna amuyunakas chiqapuni juk'ampi askichata?",
  "Download": "Descargaña",
  "Draft status": "Borrador estadopa",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Yatichañataki uñacht'awi: HMAC-SHA256 mä mayacht'ata secretompi, jisktʼawiru wakichata, tukuskiri, comprobaña atipiri licencia tokennak uñacht'ayasa. Producción tokennakax asimétrico tuqi firmatäñapawa, apstayirin taqi jaqin llavepa /.well-known/ ukan jikxatasiri.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Kimsaqallqu /topics jaljanaka jutanipxi, aka kutix mä IA agenten yatiqatapawa, jan makhatampi askichatäkiti — nayrïr arunakampi pachpa: sapa fuentex jikxatatawa ukat uñakipatawa yapaña nayraqata, resumenanakax nayrïr amuyumpi qillqatawa. Taqpacha 14 jaljanakawa.",
  "Email": "Correo electrónico",
  "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model": "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model",
  "Empirical Research": "Uñjata Yatiqäwi",
  "English edition →": "Inglés qillqata →",
  "Ensure openness is machine-executable — so goodwill is not discarded as legal uncertainty.": "Jist'arata kankañax makinanakan lurasiña atipata kankañapawa amtaña — ukhamat askinjam munañax janiw leyi tuqit jan yatit sasa apthapiskaniti.",
  "Epistemology": "Epistemología",
