  "robots.txt and llms.txt govern access and visibility, not learning depth or use permissions. AIRS proposes expressing AI rights as a proportional, use-specific spectrum across ten dimensions — access, indexing, inference input, embedding, training, fine-tuning, distillation, memory, output, attribution/compensation. AILP translates this into /ai/rights-spectrum.json, letting creators declare granular permissions with compensation models ranging from free through license-required to revenue share.": "robots.txt ukat llms.txt ukanakax mantawi ukat uñstawi apnaqi, janiw yatiqañ jach'anïri jan ukax apnaqäwi permisonakäkiti. AIRS ukax IA derechonak mä proporcional, apnaqäwiparjama espectro jinaki uñacht'ayañ amtaraki, tunka dimensionanakan — mantawi, indexación, inference input, embedding, yatichaña, askichaña, destilación, amtxatawi, mistuwi, atribución/kutt'ayawi. AILP ukax akjay /ai/rights-spectrum.json ukaru mayjt'ayaraki, luraqinakaru atisa granular permisonak yatiyañataki, kutt'ayawi modelonakampi jan pagattpach, licencia mayatatpach, askipa jaljasiñakama.",
